images.scene_prompt:
Focus: BORDERED OUTPUT TABLES. Titlebar exact "Automexia — bordered tables". One full-width terminal pane with a bright thin cyan focus outline. Prompt ribbon uses Ubuntu, main, local, demo, Docker matching the reference's powerline shapes. Path "./demo". Command spans two lines in natural terminal style: "$ docker ps --format" and "  'table {{.Names}}\t{{.Image}}\t{{.Ports}}\t{{.Status}}'". Beneath, show a large, dense, perfectly aligned native terminal table with BLUE-GRAY outer frame and individual grid lines, no rounded spreadsheet card. Headers "NAMES", "IMAGE", "PORTS", "STATUS". Five rows:
"api" | "demo/api:dev" | "8080:8080" | "Up 12 minutes (healthy)";
"web" | "nginx:alpine" | "8081:80" | "Up 12 minutes (healthy)";
"cache" | "redis:alpine" | "6379:6379" | "Up 8 minutes (healthy)";
"worker" | "demo/worker:dev" | "—" | "Up 2 minutes";
"batch" | "demo/batch:dev" | "—" | "Exited (0)".
Neutral pale cyan ordinary text; row 1-3 have very subtle green background with lime text, last two rows subtle cyan text and navy/cyan background to avoid claiming health without a health result. Table extends most of the pane width but keep text at natural terminal size and rows modest, not inflated UI tiles. Below table show another completed command "$ printf 'NAME  COUNT\napi   12\nweb   8\n'" and a small plain two-column example table "NAME | COUNT", "api | 12", "web | 8" with subtle alternating neutral navy rows. This demonstrates generic recognized header tables without implying provider tools. Finish with next prompt ribbon and idle "$" cursor. Footer within pane: "PANE 1/1 • LOCAL" left, "UTF-8 | LF" right. External bottom annotations: "1  Aligned columns" / "2  Configurable borders and separators" / "3  Original text stays copyable".
